{"title":"Keeping matters in perspective","link":"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/940871909/0/marginalrevolution~Keeping-matters-in-perspective.html","date":1768896258000,"content":"<blockquote><p>Moreover, China’s expanding leadership in scientific production has not translated into a commensurate shift in global diffusion and integration. Elite research remains disproportionately focused on US topics (40% of breakthrough publications), and citations to Chinese research disproportionately come from within China rather than from other regions, even for top-tier science.</p></blockquote>\r\n<p>That is from <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nber.org/papers/w34694\" target=\"_blank\">a new NBER working paper</a> on the geography of science, by <span><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nber.org/people/abhishek_nagaraj\">Abhishek Nagaraj</a> </span> <span> &amp; <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://www.nber.org/people/randol_yao\">Randol Yao</a>.</span></p>\r\n<p>The post <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/01/keeping-matters-in-perspective.html\">Keeping matters in perspective</a> appeared first on <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/t/0/0/marginalrevolution/~https://marginalrevolution.com\">Marginal REVOLUTION</a>.</p>\r\n<img height=\"1\" width=\"1\" src=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/~/i/940871909/0/marginalrevolution\" />\r\n<div><a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/28/940871909/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/fblike20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/29/940871909/marginalrevolution,\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/pinterest20.png\" /></a> <a href=\"https://feeds.feedblitz.com/_/24/940871909/marginalrevolution\"><img height=\"20\" src=\"https://assets.feedblitz.com/i/x